      "start_seconds": 5.74,
      "end_seconds": 9.14,
      "duration_seconds": 3.4,
      "text": "morning, doctor, sorry about the rush"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0003",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 10.5,
      "end_seconds": 14.43,
      "duration_seconds": 3.93,
      "text": "so so what can I do for you?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0004",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 15.03,
      "end_seconds": 25.67,
      "duration_seconds": 10.64,
      "text": "well, I've been having hard small stools. I thought it would sort itself out, but it hasn't"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0005",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 27.26,
      "end_seconds": 30.18,
      "duration_seconds": 2.92,
      "text": "how long has it been like this?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0006",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 33.77,
      "end_seconds": 49.31,
      "duration_seconds": 15.54,
      "text": "erm it's been about three months I'm fairly sure oh and not opening my bowels right as for not opening my bowels about a six out of ten"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0007",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 50.01,
      "end_seconds": 53.11,
      "duration_seconds": 3.1,
      "text": "have you had a lack of appetite?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0008",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 54.8,
      "end_seconds": 61.17,
      "duration_seconds": 6.37,
      "text": "yes, actually. Straining was there, but it's gone away on its own"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0009",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 62.17,
      "end_seconds": 64.9,
      "duration_seconds": 2.73,
      "text": "have you had any passing wind?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0010",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 66.01,
      "end_seconds": 68.25,
      "duration_seconds": 2.24,
      "text": "no passing wind thankfully"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0011",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 69.93,
      "end_seconds": 75.15,
      "duration_seconds": 5.22,
      "text": "And what about severe abdominal pain vomiting weight loss or black stools?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0012",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 76.33,
      "end_seconds": 79.06,
      "duration_seconds": 2.73,
      "text": "No none that I've noticed."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0013",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 80.42,
      "end_seconds": 82.71,
      "duration_seconds": 2.29,
      "text": "Is your mobility otherwise okay?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0014",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 83.5,
      "end_seconds": 85.09,
      "duration_seconds": 1.59,
      "text": "nothing else aches"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0015",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 85.67,
      "end_seconds": 88.99,
      "duration_seconds": 3.32,
      "text": "How about your heart any problems like that?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0016",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 89.89,
      "end_seconds": 95.0,
      "duration_seconds": 5.11,
      "text": "my heart's been fine, as far as I know"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0017",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 104.79,
      "end_seconds": 108.13,
      "duration_seconds": 3.34,
      "text": "Let me ask about allergies, anything at all?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0018",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 109.98,
      "end_seconds": 125.6,
      "duration_seconds": 15.62,
      "text": "mm, uh, yes, erythromycin i've no idea what the reaction was, only that I'm not supposed to have it i'm allergic to nickel, I get a rash on my skin"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0019",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 127.61,
      "end_seconds": 133.61,
      "duration_seconds": 6.0,
      "text": "Tell me your medicines, please. These questions might sound routine, but they matter."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0020",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 135.46,
      "end_seconds": 143.73,
      "duration_seconds": 8.27,
      "text": "okay, uh, so I'm on naproxen, twice a day for the knee pain"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0021",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 145.52,
      "end_seconds": 147.98,
      "duration_seconds": 2.46,
      "text": "Do you know the dose?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0022",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 148.79,
      "end_seconds": 161.52,
      "duration_seconds": 12.73,
      "text": "it's 250 milligrams. It's It's Thyronorm 50 micrograms every morning for my thyroid. I had paracetamol at one point um but I'm off it now"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0023",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 162.11,
      "end_seconds": 164.16,
      "duration_seconds": 2.05,
      "text": "do you live by yourself?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0024",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 165.89,
      "end_seconds": 170.37,
      "duration_seconds": 4.48,
      "text": "No, I share a house with my brother"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0025",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 172.14,
      "end_seconds": 173.32,
      "duration_seconds": 1.18,
      "text": "are you active?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0026",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 174.47,
      "end_seconds": 177.8,
      "duration_seconds": 3.33,
      "text": "I walk the dog every morning"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0027",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 179.65,
      "end_seconds": 182.32,
      "duration_seconds": 2.67,
      "text": "do you have any long-term conditions?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0028",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 183.29,
      "end_seconds": 201.82,
      "duration_seconds": 18.53,
      "text": "Okay, so I have arthritis in my knees, for two years. My sister suggested writing things down, but I forgot. I told myself I'd wait and see, and here I am. I've got an underactive thyroid."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0029",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 203.37,
      "end_seconds": 204.98,
      "duration_seconds": 1.61,
      "text": "is there anything more?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0030",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 209.53,
      "end_seconds": 218.45,
      "duration_seconds": 8.92,
      "text": "right so an underactive thyroid is already on your record. We'll keep that in mind today. Let me quickly check your readings"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0031",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 225.32,
      "end_seconds": 228.1,
      "duration_seconds": 2.78,
      "text": "Right bear with me while this finishes..."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0032",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 250.02,
      "end_seconds": 259.44,
      "duration_seconds": 9.42,
      "text": "Okay: pulse is 71 beats a minute temperature is 36.9 degrees. And saturation 98 percent pressure 126 over 72."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0033",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 260.71,
      "end_seconds": 262.42,
      "duration_seconds": 1.71,
      "text": "Is that normal?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0034",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 265.48,
      "end_seconds": 269.81,
      "duration_seconds": 4.33,
      "text": "they help me see the whole picture more shortly"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0035",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 270.94,
      "end_seconds": 274.59,
      "duration_seconds": 3.65,
      "text": "could you come over to the couch, please?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0036",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 275.46,
      "end_seconds": 277.6,
      "duration_seconds": 2.14,
      "text": "hold that for a second"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0037",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 290.91,
      "end_seconds": 295.87,
      "duration_seconds": 4.96,
      "text": "There is firm stool in the left lower abdomen and no mass."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0038",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 299.78,
      "end_seconds": 301.9,
      "duration_seconds": 2.12,
      "text": "you can sit up now"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0039",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 318.83,
      "end_seconds": 343.62,
      "duration_seconds": 24.79,
      "text": "okay, so my impression is this: The most likely explanation is constipation, possibly related to diet or medicines. Low fibre intake is still possible. Let's book blood tests to look into constipation. I'd rather check than guess, and this is the quickest way to know more. I'm sending you for a blood count because of constipation"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0040",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 345.72,
      "end_seconds": 370.79,
      "duration_seconds": 25.07,
      "text": "I'll start you on macrogol, 1 sachet, once a day, for two weeks. You take it it by mouth. That should help with constipation. The pharmacy will go through the details again when you pick it up. More fibre, plenty of water and a regular time on the toilet after breakfast. Have I covered everything you wanted?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0041",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 371.6,
      "end_seconds": 376.59,
      "duration_seconds": 4.99,
      "text": "Yeah, okay, that makes sense. Thanks for explaining."
    }
  ]
